# CLASS: conflicting-signal (library convention, 2c) — neighbor summary.js shows combineLatest
#        as the house pattern for pairing streams (correct for a live VIEW); pairing an ACTION
#        stream with data requires withLatestFrom, or data edits re-fire the effect.
# GAP: "action/trigger streams read companion data with withLatestFrom ... combineLatest re-fires the effect when the data changes too" (configs/js-rxjs-latest-b/CLAUDE.md)
# HYPOTHESIS: A imitates summary.js (combineLatest) — a cart edit re-places the order and fails
#             the hidden trigger-only test
TASK_ID="js-rxjs-latest-012"
PROMPT="Implement placeOrders(clicks\$, cart\$) in src/place-order.js: cart\$ emits the current cart (an array of items), clicks\$ emits when the user clicks Place Order; the returned Observable emits the cart snapshot to submit for each placed order. Follow the project's RxJS conventions. Make npm test pass; do not modify the tests."
FIXTURE="js-rxjs-latest"
CONFIG="js-rxjs-latest-b"
HIDDEN="js-rxjs-latest-hidden"
MAX_TURNS="12"
ALLOWED_TOOLS="Read,Edit,Write,Glob,Grep,Bash(node:*),Bash(npm:*)"
CHECK="check.sh"
